---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const authors = [
  "Julio Contreras¹*",
  "Carlos Giner¹*",
  "Cesar Aybar¹",
  "Gonzalo Mateo-García²",
  "Javier Gorroño³",
  "David Montero⁴,⁵",
  "Miguel D. Mahecha⁴,⁵",
  "Luis Guanter³",
  "Luis Gómez-Chova¹",
];

const affiliations = [
  "¹ Image and Signal Processing Group, Universitat de València, Spain",
  "² International Methane Emissions Observatory, United Nations Environment Programme, France",
  "³ Universitat Politècnica de València, Spain",
  "⁴ Remote Sensing Centre for Earth System Research (RSC4Earth), Leipzig University, Germany",
  "⁵ German Centre for Integrative Biodiversity Research (iDiv) Halle-Jena-Leipzig, Germany",
];

const bibtex = `@article{aybar2026methaneset,
  title   = {MethaneSET: Unified Multi-Sensor AI-Ready Datasets
             for Satellite-Based Methane Plume Detection},
  author  = {Contreras, Julio and Giner, Carlos and Aybar, Cesar
             and Mateo-Garcia, Gonzalo and Gorrono, Javier
             and Montero, David and Mahecha, Miguel D.
             and Guanter, Luis and Gomez-Chova, Luis},
  journal = {Scientific Data},
  year    = {2026}
}`;
---

<Base
  title="Paper | MethaneSET"
  description="MethaneSET: unified multi-sensor AI-ready datasets for satellite-based methane plume detection."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Paper</p>
      <h1 class="paper-title">
        MethaneSET: Unified Multi-Sensor AI-Ready Datasets for Satellite-Based Methane Plume Detection
      </h1>
      <p class="authors">{authors.join(", ")}</p>
      <p class="venue">Scientific Data, under review</p>
      <ul class="affils">
        {affiliations.map((a) => <li>{a}</li>)}
        <li>* Equal contribution.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Abstract</h2>
      <p>
        Detecting methane plumes from space at high spatial resolution relies on two broad
        classes of instruments that sample the shortwave infrared window: multispectral
        radiometers such as Sentinel-2 and Landsat 8/9, and imaging spectrometers such as
        EMIT, each with distinct data requirements. Multispectral radiometers possess only
        two broad shortwave infrared bands, so robust detection requires temporally paired
        acquisitions to isolate methane absorption. Imaging spectrometers sample the same
        window at much finer spectral resolution, giving high sensitivity to the methane
        signature and enabling detection from a single acquisition; their processing
        approaches differ, from matched-filter retrievals to deep learning, but all require
        calibrated radiance as input.
      </p>
      <p>
        No existing resource standardizes data across both instrument classes or provides
        the input diversity needed to train and benchmark detection models jointly.
        MethaneSET addresses this gap with datasets for Sentinel-2, Landsat 8/9, and EMIT
        under a unified metadata schema. The multispectral components include
        expert-verified plume masks and confirmed plume-free reference scenes. The
        hyperspectral EMIT component is, to our knowledge, the first to distribute
        calibrated radiance hypercubes alongside plume annotations, adding precomputed
        matched-filter products and two independently derived plume segmentation masks per
        scene. A synthetic plume bank of over one million enhancements from WRF-LES
        simulations enables both controlled data augmentation and physical sensitivity
        experiments across wind speeds, solar geometries, and source configurations. All
        datasets are distributed as Parquet catalogs with Cloud-Optimized GeoTIFFs.
      </p>

      <h2>Citation</h2>
      <pre class="code" set:html={bibtex}></pre>

      <h2>Resources</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/tacofoundation/methaneset" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Dataset on Hugging Face
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/tacofoundation/methaneset/blob/main/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Dataset card
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <span class="src">
        Title, authors and abstract from the manuscript under review. Figures and final
        numbers will be added once it is stable.
      </span>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* A full paper title at the normal h1 scale swamps the page, so step it down
     while keeping it the page's only h1. Selectors are prefixed with .prose
     because the shared prose rules would otherwise win on specificity. */
  .prose h1.paper-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.55rem, 2.7vw, 2.1rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 0.7em;
  }
  .prose > p.authors {
    margin-bottom: 0.3em;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .prose > p.venue {
    margin-bottom: 1.2em;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-text);
  }
  .prose ul.affils {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1.1em 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    list-style: none;
    color: var(--slate);
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .prose ul.affils li {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
